{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698324/senior-graduate-development-coordinator": {
      "title": "Senior Graduate Development Coordinator",
      "description": "Senior Graduate Development Coordinator Job No.: 698324 Location: Caulfield campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 14 month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $110,527 - $121,227 HEW 07 plus 17% employer superannuation Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The Senior Graduate Development Coordinator plays a key role in delivering tailored career advisory and enhancement services to Monash Business School students. Working closely with the Graduate Development Manager, you will coordinate a range of student-focused programs and initiatives, including career workshops, psychometric assessments, mock interviews, case interview and competition preparation, industry placements and projects, assessment centre simulations, executive coaching and mentoring. You will provide high-level administrative, event coordination and project management support across the Graduate Development program, while building strong relationships with Career Connect and other internal and external stakeholders. You will also contribute to data analysis, reporting, continuous improvement and broader projects across the Student and Education Services group. About You You will be an experienced program administrator and coordinator with a strong customer service focus and demonstrated ability to manage complex activities, projects and events. You will bring excellent organisational skills, sound judgement and the ability to establish priorities, meet deadlines and identify opportunities to improve processes and service delivery. You will have highly developed interpersonal, communication, relationship management and consulting skills, with the ability to provide specialist advice and communicate complex information effectively. Experience in careers advisory services and program delivery, preferably within a tertiary education or related environment, together with knowledge of current trends in postgraduate student employability, will be highly regarded. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Chris Keynes, Manager, Graduate Development, chris.keynes@monash.edu Position Description: Senior Graduate Development Coordinator Applications Close: Monday 26th of October 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697134/lecturer-human-geography": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Human Geography",
      "description": "Lecturer - Human Geography Job No.: 697134 Location: Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Fixed-term appointment until 30th December 2029 Remuneration: $123,138 - $146,228 pa Level B (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity Are you a researcher and dynamic educator dedicated to solving some of the world's most pressing environmental and social challenges? The School of Social Sciences is seeking a Lecturer in Human Geography to bolster our teaching and research profile in climate governance and adaptation, and community decision-making. Why Join Us? In this role, you’ll play a key part in expanding our vibrant section’s expertise, particularly across international development contexts, in research areas that explore the societal, economic and political dimensions of climate change governance, mitigation and adaptation policy and practice, and in teaching responsibilities including contributions to the Masters of International Development Practice and the new Bachelors of Climate, Society and Economy. You will join a highly collaborative, collegiate environment where your research is supported and your contribution to student learning is genuinely valued. About the Role As a Level B Lecturer in Human Geography, you’ll inspire the next generation of geographers and development specialists while advancing your own research profile. Your key responsibilities will include: Innovative Teaching and Coordination: Design, coordinate, and deliver engaging undergraduate and postgraduate units focussed on climate governance, adaptation, and international development. Student Mentorship: Lead lectures, tutorials, and field excursions, while supervising Honours and postgraduate coursework and research students. Impactful Research: Maintain and expand a strong track record of refereed publications, developing cutting-edge research in your field. Community and Collaboration: Actively contribute to the academic life of the section and school through collaborative initiatives, service duties, and engagement with external organisations. What you will Bring Qualifications: A PhD degree in Human Geography, International Development, or a closely related discipline (or equivalent accreditation and standing). Teaching Excellence: A demonstrated track record of tertiary teaching, curriculum development, and an ability to motivate and actively engage students. Research Capability: Proven commitment to scholarly research, including strong manuscript preparation, statistical analysis skills, and high-quality publications. Collegiate Spirit: Excellent interpersonal skills with a proven ability to work cooperatively across teams, students, and external partners. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Peter Searles-Adey, School of Social Sciences, Peter.Adey@monash.edu Position Description: Lecturer - Human Geography Applications Close: Tuesday 10th November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/699177/research-fellow-material-agency": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Material Agency",
      "description": "Research Fellow - Material Agency Job No.: 699177 Location: Caulfield campus Employment Type: Part-time, fraction (0.8) Duration: 1-year fixed-term appointment Remuneration: Pro-rata of $86,195 - $116,981 pa Level A (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The Faculty of Information Technology is looking for a Level A Academic Research Fellow to contribute to an Australian Research Council (ARC) Discovery Project. This collaborative initiative between Monash University’s SensiLab and RMIT University’s Tectonic Formation Lab aims to develop new design methodologies that control the spontaneous dynamics of emergent systems with the guidance of artificial intelligence techniques. The project will develop novel design processes that embed material behaviour within agent-based and machine learning computational design systems. The expected outcomes of this project include new design knowledge demonstrated through architectural and design prototypes that fuse computational design, robotic craftsmanship, and biomaterials. The successful candidate will have strong research experience in computational design and artificial intelligence. An interest in emerging creative design practice is also highly favourable. If you are excited about the opportunity to be part of a pioneering research project at the intersection of design, artificial intelligence, and material behaviour then apply today! About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Join the pursuit of our purpose to build a better future for ourselves and our communities - #ChangeIt with us. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Jon McCormack, Department of Human Centred Computing, Jon.McCormack@monash.edu Position Description: Research Fellow - Material Agency Applications Close: Tuesday 10th November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present."
